<title>SRI LANKA: S.LANKA 2-YR BONDS YIELDS FALL AT LATEST ACUTION.</title>
<headline>S.LANKA 2-YR BONDS YIELDS FALL AT LATEST ACUTION.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on two-year Treasury Bonds fell to 11.87 percent at the latest auction on Tuesday, the Central bank said.</p>
<p>It said the 500 million rupees bond issue with a coupon rate of 12.5 percent per annum was heavily oversubscribed.</p>
<p>				   Current	Previous</p>
<p>    Amoung offered	   500 million	500 million</p>
<p>    Bids received	   2,910 million    3,365 million</p>
<p>    Amount accepted	  500 million	500 million</p>
<p>    Weighted avg yield	11.87%	 12.42%</p>
<p>    Yield range	    11.51%-11.99%  12.42%-12.43%</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
